From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:57:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Run debugger.js on QuickJS

servo-quickjs now emulates SpiderMonkey's Debugger API, so the debugger
global defines it and runs debugger.js on QuickJS too. Before, console
evaluations, autocompletion and source lists of the QuickJS build waited
forever for debugger.js to reply. While paused, each devtools message
releases what it kept alive in QuickJS's autorelease pool.

The servo-quickjs pin moves from ae9eb96, where JS_DefineDebuggerObject
is a stub that panics, to 6ac4a17, which has the emulation. servo-quickjs
builds it, and QuickJS's patches for debuggers, only when asked, and
Servo can't enable a feature of it that SpiderMonkey's mozjs doesn't
have. So mach sets SERVO_QUICKJS_DEBUGGER=1 for QuickJS builds that may
have the devtools feature, and 0 for those without default features
that select no feature enabling it, which get none of the debugger code.
The QuickJS Cargo configuration defaults the variable to 1 for Cargo
commands run without mach.

Validation: QuickJS builds against servo-quickjs 48bd1fc, the same tree as 6ac4a17 before it was merged: `./mach test-devtools` passes 102 tests with 7 expected failures in release and checked-release, the same tests as SpiderMonkey on this base (release build of the 2026-11-09 sync). A QuickJS release build without devtools (the default features but `default_tooling`, so `SERVO_QUICKJS_DEBUGGER=0`) has neither the emulation nor QuickJS's debugger code, and like the build with devtools runs a page with an external script (compiled off the main thread) and a dedicated worker. `may_have_devtools` gives 1 for the arguments of ohos-device-wpt.yml's QuickJS build (`--no-default-features --features "base ohos-rdb-backend"`) and for `-Fbase`, and 0 without default features and devtools; `[env]` in a Cargo configuration file sets the variable when the environment doesn't.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested by the agent, reviewed by another agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
